From: TrailCurrent
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: dragon-q6a: Enable I2C6 for the GNSS receiver

The Godwit head unit has a GNSS receiver on header pins 3 and 5, which are
QUP0 SE6 (i2c6). The board DT leaves that bus disabled; enable it at
100 kHz so the receiver can be read through i2c-dev, with the pins' internal
pull-ups on, as the Bearing firmware drives the same receiver.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board-specific: Godwit header wiring]

---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qcs6490-radxa-dragon-q6a.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qcs6490-radxa-dragon-q6a.dts
@@ -547,6 +547,17 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+/* GNSS receiver on header pins 3 (SDA) and 5 (SCL), read from userspace */
+&i2c6 {
+	clock-frequency = <100000>;
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&qup_i2c6_data_clk {
+	bias-pull-up;
+	drive-strength = <2>;
+};
+
 /* External touchscreen */
 &i2c13 {
 	qcom,enable-gsi-dma;
